# Build artifacts
/bin/
/dist/
/out/
*.exe
*.test
*.out

# Python bytecode. The AI runtime targets 3.11+ and the standard library only,
# so a committed .pyc is a build artifact that pins an interpreter nobody else
# runs, and it gets stale silently.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Test and coverage output. `go test -coverprofile=coverage` writes a plain
# file at the repo root, which is easy to stage by accident.
/coverage
/coverage.*

# Local runtime state — never commit evidence, logs, secrets or checkpoints
/data/
/evidence/
/logs/
/secrets/
/checkpoints/
*.key
*.pem

# Replay fixtures captured from a live system may contain real site data.
# Sanitized, reviewed fixtures only. The sanitiser is the single choke point
# between a live source and a committed file: internal/fixture/sanitize.go.
# See internal/README.md.
/fixtures/private/
/testdata/private/

# Downloaded footage of somebody else's camera, at the repository root or under
# `poc/active-monitoring`. Every clip here is unrecorded licence and several are
# 96-294 MB; `testdata/labels.json` names the clips that may be committed and
# none of these are among them. See poc/active-monitoring/.gitignore for the
# same rule inside the module.
/testdata/live/
/poc/*/testdata/live/
/record*.log

# Tooling
/tools/bin/
/.protoc/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store

# The agent's own workspace state. Not part of the product: it is machine-local,
# it changes on every run, and committing it makes every diff noisy for whoever
# reads the repository.
#
# The exclusion is `.kilo/*` rather than `.kilo/` so that `.kilo/skills/` can be
# un-ignored below. Git does not descend into an excluded directory, so a blanket
# `.kilo/` makes the negation impossible and the repo-local skills would exist
# only on this machine.
#
# `.kilo/skills/` is the exception because a skill in it is not workspace state.
# It encodes an invariant from AGENTS.md as a procedure, and `AGENTS.md` reserves
# changing an invariant to a human who reads the diff. A skill that is not
# committed is a skill no human ever signs off on.
.kilo/*
!.kilo/skills/

# Python bytecode from the AI runtime tests
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Model weights. 114 MB, over GitHub's 100 MB blob limit, and downloaded rather
# than built: the download command is in the detector's own documentation, so a
# committed .pt pins a binary that no build step reproduces and that every clone
# pays for.
/yolo11x.pt

# The POC's local Python virtualenv. yt-dlp, NumPy and SciPy in site-packages
# are a machine's install, not the product's source, and the whole tree is
# megabytes of DLLs that differ per interpreter.
/.venv-poc/

# Runtime spill from a POC run, written at the repository root by the demos and
# the live server: one incident artifact and one observation per detected event.
# They are local state with a storage reference in them, not a fixture, and the
# sanitised fixtures belong in internal/fixture.
/inc_*.incident.json
/inc_*.observation.json

# A `go tool cover -func` invocation whose redirect was mistyped, which left its
# output at the repository root instead of in a file it named.
/$f

# A vendor tool's own workspace state.
/.freebuff/

# A scratch copy of the POC config's Go type declarations, kept next to the code
# it was copied from while that code was being rewritten.
/poc/config_types_restore.txt

# The operator's own footage. `Videos/` holds 375 MB of MP4 that the demo plays
# as virtual cameras. It is the owner's material and not the repository's: a
# clone does not need it, and a commit that carries it makes every diff carry
# it. The demo script references it by path and says so when it is absent.
/Videos/

# Another project entirely, which was sitting in this working tree. It is not
# part of this product, and it must never enter this history.
/product-scraper/

# The SPA's build output. `npm run build` in web/spa writes it; the source that
# produces it is committed. A committed bundle is a binary that no build step
# reproduces and that every clone pays for.
/web/spa/node_modules/
/web/spa/playwright-report/
/web/spa/test-results/
/web/static/spa/

# Editor and tooling backups. A `.bak` file is a copy of a file that is already
# in the history, and it goes stale the moment the original changes.
*.bak
*.bak2